abilities and access updated libraries. *(Note: The exam environment mitigates this by providing frozen, pre-installed library versions guaranteed to work with 3.7).*\n2. **Performance Optimizations:** Recent Python versions (especially 3.11 onwards) include a \"Faster CPython\" project, which significantly speeds up code execution. While shaving milliseconds off a Bubble Sort is irrelevant in an A-Level exam, it drastically reduces server costs in enterprise web applications.\n3. **Advanced Language Features:** Modern Python introduces features like strict type hinting and asynchronous I/O (`async`/`await`). These are essential for writing scalable, enterprise-grade software, but they fall completely outside the scope of the H2 Computing syllabus. \n\n**Bottom Line:** Downgrade your practice environment to Python 3.7. Master the syllabus fundamentals using the constraints you will face on exam day.",
