    }, {
      "text": "If the browser sends a `GET` request on initial load but \"ignores\" your button click, it means **the form submission is failing to trigger** or **the request is being lost in the browser**.\n\nHere is the checklist to diagnose why your `POST` request is disappearing:\n\n### 1. The \"Ghost\" Form (Button Placement)\nThe most common cause for \"nothing happening\" when you click a button is that the button is not technically a \"submit\" type or is malformed.\n*   **The Fix:** Ensure your button is explicitly typed: `\u003cinput type\u003d\"submit\" value\u003d\"Submit\"\u003e` or `\u003cbutton type\u003d\"submit\"\u003eSubmit\u003c/button\u003e`.\n*   **Check:** Is your button placed **inside** the `\u003cform\u003e ... \u003c/form\u003e` tags? If it is outside, clicking it does nothing.\n\n### 2. Form Submission Interception (JavaScript)\nSometimes, modern browser extensions or accidental JavaScript can intercept the \"Submit\" event. \n*   **The Fix:** Check your terminal output. \n    *   If you click the button and **no new log line** appears in your Flask terminal, the request **never reached the server**. \n    *   If no request reaches the server, the problem is 100% in your HTML (the form isn\u0027t actually submitting).\n\n### 3. The `action` Attribute\nIf your `action` is pointing to a route that doesn\u0027t exist, the browser might be trying to submit the request, failing, and just staying on the current page.\n*   **The Fix:** Look at the URL in your Chrome address bar after you click the button. \n    *   Does it change to something like `http://127.0.0.1:5000/?`? \n    *   If you see a `?` at the end of your URL, your form is defaulting to `GET` (you missed `method\u003d\"POST\"` in the HTML). \n    *   **Force the target:** Change your HTML form to explicitly target the route:\n        ```html\n        \u003cform method\u003d\"POST\" action\u003d\"/\"\u003e\n        ```\n\n### 4. The \"Hard Refresh\" Trap\nFlask servers and Chrome browsers often \"cache\" (remember) old versions of your files. You might be clicking a button on a version of the HTML that no longer matches your current code.\n*   **The Fix:** \n    1.  Close your browser tab completely.\n    2.  Stop the Flask server in your terminal (`Ctrl+C`).\n    3.  Restart the Flask server.\n    4.  Open a new tab and go to the URL again.\n\n### 5. Debugging with the Network Tab (The \"Smoking Gun\")\nYou don\u0027t need to guess why it\u0027s not working. Chrome can show you exactly what is happening:\n1.  In Chrome, press **F12** to open Developer Tools.\n2.  Click the **Network** tab.\n3.  Click your \"Submit\" button.\n4.  **Look at the Network tab:**\n    *   **If nothing appears:** Your HTML form is broken; it\u0027s not attempting to send anything. Check your `\u003cform\u003e` tag and `\u003cinput type\u003d\"submit\"\u003e`.\n    *   **If a request appears (marked in red):** Click on it. Look at the \"Headers\" tab to see the Request Method. If it says `GET` instead of `POST`, your HTML `method` attribute is ignored/wrong. If it says `405`, your Python `@app.route` decorator is missing `methods\u003d[\u0027POST\u0027]`.\n\n### Summary of the \"Golden\" HTML/Python Pair\nIf you are still stuck, delete your current HTML/Python logic and replace it with this minimal pair to see if it works:\n\n**HTML:**\n```html\n\u003cform method\u003d\"POST\" action\u003d\"/\"\u003e\n    \u003cinput type\u003d\"text\" name\u003d\"test\"\u003e\n    \u003cinput type\u003d\"submit\" value\u003d\"Click Me\"\u003e\n\u003c/form\u003e\n```\n\n**Python:**\n```python\n@app.route(\u0027/\u0027, methods\u003d[\u0027GET\u0027, \u0027POST\u0027])\ndef index():\n    if request.method \u003d\u003d \u0027POST\u0027:\n        print(\"POST RECEIVED!\") # Check your terminal for this!\n        return \"It works!\"\n    return render_template(\u0027your_file.html\u0027)\n```\nIf this minimal version works, copy your logic back in piece by piece until it breaks—that will reveal the exact line causing the issue.",
