 *URL* matches but the *Method* (GET/POST) is wrong.\n*   **A `500 Internal Server Error`** (which you got) means the request was accepted and the route was matched, but your **Python code crashed** while trying to run. \n\n**Pro-Tip for Debugging:** Whenever you see `TypeError: ... missing 1 required positional argument` in Flask, it is almost always a mismatch between the `\u003cvariable\u003e` inside your `@app.route()` string and the `(variable)` inside your `def function()` statement. Ensure these names are always identical.",
