l\u003eRemarks:\u003c/label\u003e\n\u003ctextarea name\u003d\"remarks\" rows\u003d\"4\" cols\u003d\"50\"\u003e\u003c/textarea\u003e\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. CSS: The \"Layout\" Toolbox\nYou don\u0027t need to be a designer. You need to know how to create **tables** and **containers** to present your data cleanly.\n\n**A. Centering and Spacing (The \"Exam Container\"):**\nEvery task asks for a \"bordered container.\" Memorise this:\n```css\n.container {\n    width: 600px;\n    margin: 50px auto; /* Centers the container */\n    padding: 20px;\n    border: 2px solid #2F8A7B; /* Exam standard color */\n    background-color: white;\n}\n```\n\n**B. Table Presentation:**\nTables are the default way to show database `SELECT` results.\n```css\ntable {\n    width: 100%;\n    border-collapse: collapse; /* Prevents double lines */\n}\nth, td {\n    border: 1px solid black;\n    padding: 8px;\n    text-align: center;\n}\nth {\n    background-color: #2F8A7B; /* Distinct header row */\n    color: white;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Advanced Jinja2: Loops and Logic\nPractical papers often require you to display a table only if data exists, and show a message if it doesn\u0027t. \n\n**The \"If-Else\" Pattern:**\n```html\n{% if results %}\n    \u003ctable\u003e\n        ...\n    \u003c/table\u003e\n{% else %}\n    \u003cp\u003eNo records found for your search.\u003c/p\u003e\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Your Progression Task (The \"Mastery\" Project)\n\nTo prove you have mastered the remainder of the syllabus, create a **\"Latecoming Search\"** application. It must do the following:\n\n1.  **Home (`/`):** A form with a dropdown (`select`) for `Category` (\u0027Medical\u0027, \u0027Family\u0027) and a text box for the student\u0027s name.\n2.  **Process (`/search`):** A `POST` route that:\n    *   Retrieves the data.\n    *   Queries your SQLite/MongoDB for matches.\n    *   If matches exist, renders `results.html` with a table.\n    *   If no matches exist, renders `results.html` with th