      "text": "### Part 1: Are You Ready?\n\nYou are **extremely close** to being completely ready. Your full-stack flow is logical, the dynamic header mapping is clever, and your redirect logic is structurally correct. \n\nHowever, there are a few **critical database and syntax bugs** that would break your application in an exam or cause silent data loss.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Bugs to Fix\n\n#### 1. The SQLite Primary Key Conflict (Silent Data Loss)\nIn `app.py`, you defined `Student_ID` as the `PRIMARY KEY` of the `late` table:\n```python\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS late (\n    {headers[0]} TEXT,\n    {headers[1]} INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,  -- Student_ID is the PK\n    ...\n)\n```\n* **The Bug:** A `PRIMARY KEY` column must be completely unique. If a student is late more than once (e.g., student `25092` is late on 2024-07-03, 2024-08-01, etc.), your `INSERT OR IGNORE` statement will silently **ignore and discard** all subsequent latecomer records for that student.\n* **The Fix:** Remove `PRIMARY KEY` from `Student_ID` in the `late` table. Instead, let SQLite assign its own internal ID, or use a composite key of `(Date, Student_ID)`.\n\n#### 2. CSS Syntax Violations\nIn `style.css`, you have a few syntax errors that browsers will ignore (meaning your styles won\u0027t load):\n* **Space in Units:** `width: 800 px;` must be `width: 800px;` (no spaces allowed).\n* **Incorrect Hash Symbol on Named Colors:** `#black`, `#white`, and `#red` are incorrect. Named colors do not use a `#` (hash). It should be `black`, `white`, and `red`.\n* **Invalid padding values:** `padding: auto;` or `padding: 20px auto;` are invalid. `auto` is only valid for margins. Use explicit values like `padding: 10px;`.\n\n#### 3. HTML Structural Errors\nIn `results.html`:\n* **The `\u003cbody\u003e` container wrap:** Your `div` wraps your `body`. This violates HTML standards. The `\u003cbody\u003e` should always wrap your `\u003cdiv class\u003d\"container\"\u003e`.\n* **Missing `\u003ctr\u003e` and unclosed tags:** In `results.html`, you are missing closing `\u003c/tr\u003e` tags in your table header and a starting `\u003ctr\u003e` tag inside your table body loop.\n\n---\n\n### Part 2: Your Quick Questions Answered\n\n#### Q1: Can I pass and render an HTML string through `render_template` using `{{ }}`?\n**Yes, but with one crucial step.**\nBy default, Jinja2 automatically escapes HTML tags to protect against script injection. If you pass `my_html \u003d \"\u003ch1\u003eHello\u003c/h1\u003e\"`, Jinja will output the literal text `\u003ch1\u003eHello\u003c/h1\u003e` on the screen.\n\nTo tell Jinja to render it as raw HTML, you must append the **`safe`** filter [S4D, 20]:\n```html\n{{ my_html | safe }}\n```\n\n#### Q2: Why is it good practice to run the app inside `if __name__ \u003d\u003d \u0027__main__\u0027:`?\nWhen a Python file is run directly, its internal variable `__name__` is set to `\"__main__\"`. \n\nIf another script (like a test suite or a production WSGI server like Gunicorn) imports your `app.py`, Python executes the entire file. Without this `if` guard, **the Flask server would boot up during import**, blocking the external program or test suite from running.\n\n#### Q3: What is `student.Student_Name LIKE ?` and `(f\"%{name}%\")`?\n* **`LIKE`:** This is SQL\u0027s pattern-matching operator (substring search). Unlike `\u003d`, which requires an exact match, `LIKE` matches partial text.\n* **`%` Wildcard:** The `%` character represents \"zero or more characters\". \n* **`%name%`:** By wrapping the user input in percent signs, you are searching for any student whose name **contains** that input *anywhere* inside it. \n  * *Example:* If a user inputs `\"Wei\"`, `LIKE %Wei%` will successfully match `\"Chen Wei Li\"`.\n\n---\n\n### Refactored Codes (With Fixes Applied)\n\n#### Optimized `app.py`\n```python\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, url_for\nimport sqlite3, csv\n\napp \u003d Flask(__name__)\naccepted_methods \u003d [\u0027GET\u0027, \u0027POST\u0027]\n\n# Clean DB on launch\nconn \u003d sqlite3.connect(\"database.db\")\ncur \u003d conn.cursor()\ncur.execute(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS student\")\ncur.execute(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS late\")\n\n# 1. Import Students\nwith open(\"STUDENT.csv\") as file:\n    reader \u003d csv.reader(file)\n    headers \u003d next(reader)\n    cur.execute(f\"\"\"\n        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS student (\n            {headers[0]} INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n            {headers[1]} TEXT,\n            {headers[2]} TEXT,\n            {headers[3]} INTEGER\n        )\n    \"\"\")\n    for row in reader:\n        cur.execute(f\"INSERT OR IGNORE INTO student ({\u0027, \u0027.join(headers)}) VALUES(?,?,?,?)\", row)\n\n# 2. Import Late Records (Fixed Student_ID Primary Key Bug)\nwith open(\"LATE.csv\") as file:\n    reader \u003d csv.reader(file)\n    headers_late \u003d next(reader)\n    cur.execute(f\"\"\"\n        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS late (\n            {headers_late[0]} TEXT,\n            {headers_late[1]} INTEGER, -- Removed PRIMARY KEY constraint to allow duplicates\n            {headers_late[2]} TEXT,\n            FOREIGN KEY({headers_late[1]}) REFERENCES student({headers[0]})\n        )\n    \"\"\")\n    for row in reader:\n        cur.execute(f\"INSERT INTO late ({\u0027, \u0027.join(headers_late)}) VALUES (?,?,?)\", row)\n\nconn.commit()\nconn.close()\nprint(\"Data seeded successfully.\")\n\n@app.route(\u0027/\u0027, methods\u003daccepted_methods)\ndef home():\n    error \u003d None\n    if request.method \u003d\u003d \u0027POST\u0027:\n        category \u003d request.form.get(\u0027category\u0027, \u0027\u0027).strip()\n        name \u003d request.form.get(\u0027name\u0027, \u0027\u0027).strip()\n\n        if name and category:\n            return redirect(url_for(\u0027results_route\u0027, category\u003dcategory, name\u003dname))\n        else:\n            error \u003d \"Please fill in all fields\"\n    return render_template(\u0027home.html\u0027, error\u003derror)\n\n@app.route(\u0027/results/\u003ccategory\u003e/\u003cname\u003e\u0027)\ndef results_route(category, name):\n    conn \u003d sqlite3.connect(\"database.db\")\n    conn.row_factory \u003d sqlite3.Row\n    cur \u003d conn.cursor()\n\n    cur.execute(\"\"\"\n        SELECT student.Student_Name, student.Class_Group, late.Date, late.Reason\n        FROM student \n        INNER JOIN late ON student.Student_ID \u003d late.Student_ID\n        WHERE student.Student_Name LIKE ? AND late.Reason \u003d ?\n    \"\"\", (f\"%{name}%\", category))\n    data \u003d cur.fetchall()\n    conn.close()\n    return render_template(\"results.html\", results\u003ddata, category\u003dcategory, name\u003dname)\n\nif __name__ \u003d\u003d \u0027__main__\u0027:\n    app.run(port\u003d6767, debug\u003dTrue)\n```\n\n#### Corrected `style.css`\n```css\n.container {\n    width: 800px; /* Fixed space bug */\n    margin: 50px auto; /* Centered on page */\n    padding: 20px;\n    border: 2px solid black; /* Removed hash from color name */\n    background-color: #4682b4;\n    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n}\n\ntable, th, td {\n    border: 1px solid black; /* Removed hash from color name */\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    padding: 8px; /* Changed auto to explicit px spacing */\n}\n\nlabel, input, select {\n    display: block;\n    width: 100%;\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\ninput[type\u003d\"submit\"] {\n    background-color: white; /* Removed hash */\n    color: black;\n    padding: 10px;\n    border: 1px solid black;\n    cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.disclaimer {\n    color: red; /* Removed hash */\n    font-style: italic; /* Fixed font-weight \u0027italic\u0027 to font-style */\n    font-size: 10px;\n}\n```\n\n#### Corrected `results.html`\n```html\n\u003c!doctype html\u003e\n\u003chtml\u003e\n\u003chead\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eResults\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003clink rel\u003d\"stylesheet\" href\u003d\"{{ url_for(\u0027static\u0027, filename\u003d\u0027style.css\u0027) }}\"\u003e\n\u003c/head\u003e\n\u003cbody\u003e \u003c!-- Moved body tag to wrap the container --\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class\u003d\"container\"\u003e\n        \u003ch1\u003eResults\u003c/h1\u003e\n        \u003cp\u003eSearch results for \u003cb\u003e{{ name }}\u003c/b\u003e under \u003cb\u003e\"{{ category }}\"\u003c/b\u003e category\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003cp class\u003d\"disclaimer\"\u003eSorting by category does not work as backend is not equipped with category sorting logic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n        {% if results %}\n        \u003ctable\u003e\n            \u003cthead\u003e\n                \u003ctr\u003e \u003c!-- Added starting tr tag --\u003e\n                    \u003cth\u003eStudent Name\u003c/th\u003e\n                    \u003cth\u003eClass Group\u003c/th\u003e\n                    \u003cth\u003eDate\u003c/th\u003e\n                    \u003cth\u003eReason\u003c/th\u003e\n                \u003c/tr\u003e \u003c!-- Closed row correctly --\u003e\n            \u003c/thead\u003e\n            \u003ctbody\u003e\n                {% for row in results %}\n                \u003ctr\u003e \u003c!-- Added missing starting tr tag --\u003e\n                    \u003ctd\u003e{{ row[\u0027Student_Name\u0027] }}\u003c/td\u003e \u003c!-- Changed th to td for table body --\u003e\n                    \u003ctd\u003e{{ row[\u0027Class_Group\u0027] }}\u003c/td\u003e\n                    \u003ctd\u003e{{ row[\u0027Date\u0027] }}\u003c/td\u003e\n                    \u003ctd\u003e{{ row[\u0027Reason\u0027] }}\u003c/td\u003e\n                \u003c/tr\u003e\n                {% endfor %}\n            \u003c/tbody\u003e\n        \u003c/table\u003e\n        {% else %}\n        \u003cp\u003eNo latecoming records match the query.\u003c/p\u003e \n        {% endif %}\n\n        \u003cform method\u003d\"GET\" action\u003d\"/\"\u003e\n            \u003cinput type\u003d\"submit\" value\u003d\"Return to Homepage\"\u003e\n        \u003c/form\u003e\n    \u003c/div