form[\u0027dropdown\u0027]\n    ```\n\n#### 2. Variable Routing Parameter Mismatch\n**Your Blurt:** \n`@app.route(\"/\u003cuser_input\u003e/\u003cdropdown\u003e\", methods\u003dAC)`\n`def result(thingy, kusa):`\n**Why it\u0027s fatal:** Flask matches the variables in the `\u003c \u003e` directly to the function parameters. If the names don\u0027t match exactly, Flask throws a 500 Server Error (`TypeError: result() got unexpected keyword arguments`).\n**The Fix:** \n`def result(user_input, dropdown):`\n\n#### 3. HTML Table Structure Missing `\u003ctd\u003e`\n**Your Blurt:** `\u003ctr\u003e {{row[0]}} \u003c/tr\u003e`\n**Why it\u0027s fatal:** A `\u003ctr\u003e` (Table Row) tag *cannot* hold text directly. If you omit the `\u003ctd\u003e` (Table Data/cell) tags, the browser will panic and dump all your data outside the table. Your CSS borders will not apply, and it will look like a broken mess.\n**The Fix:** \n```html\n\u003ctr\u003e \n    \u003ctd\u003e{{ row[0] }}\u003c/td\u003e \n    \u003ctd\u003e{{ row[1] }}\u003c/td\u003e \n\u003c/tr\u003e\n```\n\n#### 4. CSV Parsing Logic\n**Your Blurt:** `With open(\"filename.csv\") as reader: Thead \u003d next(reader)`\n**Why it\u0027s fatal:** `open()` just returns a raw text file object. If you call `next()` on it, you get a giant un-split string (e.g., `\"ID,Name,Class\\n\"`), not a list (`[\u0027ID\u0027, \u0027Name\u0027, \u0027Class\u0027]`). Your dynamic SQL will break completely.\n**The Fix:** You forgot to invoke the `csv` module.\n```python\nwith open(\"filename.csv\") as file:\n    reader \u003d csv.reader(file)  # MUST DO THIS\n    Thead \u003d next(reader)       # Now it\u0027s a list!\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ CATEGORY 2: MINOR GAPS (Bridgeable DURING the Exam via Debugging)\n*You don\u0027t need to stress about memorising these perfectly. If you make these mistakes, the IDE/Browser will yell at you, and you can quickly fix them.*\n\n**1. `@app.route(action\u003d\"/\")`**\n*   **What will happen:** Python will immediately crash on startup with `TypeError: route() got an unexpected keyword argument \u0027action\u0027`.\n*   **How to fix in exam:** Remove `action\u003d`. It’s just `@app.route(\"/\")`.\n\n**2. SQL Syntax Typos in `CREATE TABLE`**\n*   **Your Blurt:** \n    ```sql\n    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS table_name\n    {thead[0]} INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    ```\n*   **What will happen:** Missing parentheses `()` around the columns, and missing commas `,` at the ends of lines. `sqlite3.OperationalError` will trigger, telling you exactly which line failed.\n*   **How to fix in exam:** Read the traceback, add the `(` and `,`.\n\n**3. CSS Class Selector Missing the Dot `.`**\n*   **Your Blurt:** `Error{ color: red; }`\n*   **What will happen:** Your error message won\u0027t turn red. \n*   **How to fix in exam:** You look at the browser, see it\u0027s not red, realise you meant `\u003cp class\u003d\"error\"\u003e`, and change the CSS to `.error { color: red; }`. \n\n**4. `\u003ctail\u003e` tag in HTML**\n*   **Your Blurt:** `\u003ctail\u003e ... \u003c/tail\u003e`\n*   **What will happen:** Nothing. Browsers are very forgiving and will just render the text at the bottom. But `\u003ctail\u003e` isn\u0027t real HTML (you mean `\u003cfooter\u003e`). \n*   **How to fix in exam:** Leave it or change it to `\u003cdiv\u003e`. It won\u0027t cost you marks unless it breaks the layout.\n\n---\n\n### Your Final Checklist Before Friday\n1.  **Forms use `request.form`:** Memorize that HTML forms send data to Python via `request.form[\u0027input_name\u0027]`. Do not try to inject Jinja `{{ }}` variables into the `action\u003d\"\"` attribute to pass form data.\n2.  **Tables use `\u003ctd\u003e`:** Never put data directly inside a `\u003ctr\u003e`.\n3.  **CSV needs `csv.reader`:** You cannot parse a CSV without wrapping the open file in `csv.reader()`.\n\nIf you lock down those three concepts today, your brain dump proves you have enough knowledge to easily score an A on the practical paper.",
